  - Root cause (verified on-chain, read-only): rent-exempt minimum is 0.00148844 SOL per token account.
    (1) live/src/jup.ts buildIncrease closed the owner's wSOL ATA at the end of EVERY open/add (createCloseAccountInstruction).
        The next SOL TP placement / sweep re-created it and paid the rent again: ETH sweep BvycSChw (21:06) re-created wSOL ATA
        HiCoAL (+0.00148844 parked); the 20:42 ETH/BTC opens and the 21:15 SOL open (3EgcEg) had closed it.
    (2) The per-trade ledger counted that rent as a loss: position flows counted only native + wSOL lamports, so the USDC ATA
        AJduc1 created by the ETH TP placement 2Vq4m85G (20:42, -0.00148844) and the WBTC ATA 9SQT8Y (BTC TP placement) were
        trade costs; the sweep counted only native + wrapped atoms, so the re-created wSOL ATA rent was a swap cost.
    The USDC/WBTC ATAs were NOT closed by swaps (Jupiter never closes the input account); Jupiter's wrapAndUnwrapSol cleanup does
    close the wSOL ATA on every SOL-output swap (SPL wSOL can only be unwrapped by closing), but buildSwap re-creates it in the
    same tx, so that is rent-neutral once the ATA is persistent.
